Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(web): select assets and act on whole stacks in the
 asset viewer

The asset viewer can mark and unmark the asset on screen in the shared
multi-select selection (x or the select button), clear the marks
(Ctrl+D), trash or delete the marked set (Ctrl+Delete,
Ctrl+Shift+Delete), and offer the other marked-set actions in a menu.
Marks survive leaving the viewer, and a timeline selection shows when it
opens.

While Select whole stack is on (Shift+S in the viewer), viewer trash,
download, share, album, tag, favorite and archive actions apply to every
member of the stack on screen. Membership is refreshed before acting and
the action aborts when the lookup fails. Labels state the asset count.
The toggle now stays on until the page changes. With the toggle off,
viewer actions behave as upstream.
